{"type":"message","id":"142bb976","parentId":"c1d1a15e","timestamp":"2026-02-18T12:55:48.233Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to create the environment-specific configuration for each agent. Let me also create a basic AGENTS.md file in the main workspace-generalist directory that describes the agent system.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5954862955224cd78d1b0178","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# OpenClaw Agent System\n\n## Available Agents\n\n### Primary Agents\n- **Pluto** 🪐 - Main orchestration agent, coordinates between specialists\n- **Coder** 👨‍💻 - Primary coding assistant\n- **Coder 2** 🤖 - Secondary coding assistant (duplicate setup for redundancy/testing)\n\n## Workspace Structure\n```\nD:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\\n├── config\\\n│   └── agents.list          # Main agent configuration\n├── workspace-generalist\\    # This workspace (for general tasks)\n├── workspace-pluto\\         # Pluto agent workspace\n├── workspace-coder\\         # Coder agent workspace  \n└── workspace-coder2\\        # Coder 2 agent workspace\n```\n\n## Agent Configuration\nEach agent has:\n- `SOUL.md` - Agent identity and capabilities\n- `USER.md` - User interaction guidelines\n- `agent.config.json` - Technical configuration\n- Workspace-specific files and memory\n\n## Agent Communication\n- Agents can communicate via message tool\n- Subagent permissions controlled via `allowAgents`\n- Pluto can coordinate with all coding agents\n- Coding agents can receive tasks from Pluto\n\n## Model Assignments\n- Coding agents: `arcee-ai/trinity-large-preview:free`\n- Orchestrator: `openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528:free`\n\n---\n*Last updated: 2026-02-18*","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-generalist\\AGENTS.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":17340,"output":447,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalT